        <h2>Lesson 4</h2>

        <h3>Division</h3>
        <p>
          Division is a method of splitting a total amount into smaller or equal parts. It is represnted with the ÷ symbol or the forward slash /. Division is the inverse of multiplication, and portrays the grouping/sharing of numbers, which can often result in a remainder if the calculation is not slit up equally.
        </p>

        <h3>Key Terminology</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Dividend</strong> – the specific number that is being divided</li>
          <li><strong>Divisor</strong> – the specific number that is dividing by</li>
          <li><strong>Quotient</strong> – the final answer</li>
          <li><strong>Remainder</strong> – what is remaining after division</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Worked examples</h3>
        <p><strong>Example 1:</strong> 15 ÷ 5 = 3</p>
        <p><strong>Example 2:</strong> 144 ÷ 12 = 12</p>
        <p><strong>Example 3:</strong> 21 ÷ 5 = 4 remainder 1</p>
